### Auth Service — manual API tests
### Use the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client): click "Send Request".
### Or copy these as curl commands.

@authUrl = http://localhost:5001

### 1. Register a new user
# Returns 200 with a JWT token on success, or 409 if username/email exists.
POST {{authUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "student",
  "email": "student@lab.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### 2. Login
# @name login   <-- names this response so we can reuse its token below.
POST {{authUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "student",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### 3. Copy the token from the login response.
# In REST Client you can reference it automatically:
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### 4. (Negative test) Login with a wrong password -> 401 Unauthorized
POST {{authUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "student",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### 5. Health check
GET {{authUrl}}/health
